  "design": {
    "decision": "Buy cheap [♦] low cards for length over other cards, and in a round where the team holds seven, bid knowing the multiplier is locked in. The swap enabler moves [♦]s to whoever needs them, because holdings count after Opening.",
    "opponent": "Revealed at the start of play in the rounds it fires. A team that is long in [♦] tells opponents to void [♦] and trump.",
    "rationale": "This is the [♦] mirror of the kept ua-spade-seven-x, the departure from the near-duplicate guideline that the brief asks for: [♦] holding pieces with no contract scaling. The [♦] holding line has commons (+5 per card, +30 at eight) and a per-card +mult, but no ×multiplier at uncommon. A team expects 6.5 [♦]s, so seven fires a little under half the time with no investment, and [♦] card purchases push it higher. That gives the shop a clear target without a threshold-only gimmick.",
